<div class="markdown">
    <h2>What's this?</h2>

    <p>
        The Spankscuary Webring is a hand-built neighbourhood for spanking stories,
        art, history, humour, blogs, archives, and community. It connects independently
        owned sites so readers can move from one to another without relying on search
        engines, social media feeds, or recommendation algorithms.
    </p>

    <p>
        <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Webring">Webrings</a> are an
        <a href="https://brisray.com/web/webring-history.htm">old idea</a>
        we're bringing back because they still solve a useful problem. Each member
        site links to the ring, making it possible to discover other sites through
        people rather than platforms. There are good reasons
        <a href="https://www.base31.org/blog/bringing-back-the-webring">webrings and blogrolls are making a comeback</a>:
        human curation, direct connections between independent sites, and the chance
        to stumble onto interesting things an algorithm might never show you.
    </p>

    <h2>How to join</h2>

    <p>
        Spankscuary is for independently maintained sites with substantial
        spanking-related content. Personal sites, blogs, story archives, art sites,
        history projects, forums, and other community resources are all welcome.
    </p>

    <p>
        If you have a GitHub account, you can
        <a href="{{ meta.repo }}/compare">open a pull request</a>
        with the name and URL of your site. If your site has an RSS or Atom feed
        and you know the address, please include that too.
    </p>

    <p>
        Don't use GitHub? That's fine. Just
        <a href="https://mijasroom.net/contact/">email Mija</a>.
        I'm the person currently tending Spankscuary and adding new member sites.
        If you don't know what an RSS feed is, don't worry about it. I can probably
        find it for you.
    </p>

    <p>
        When your site has been added to Spankscuary, I'll let you know and send
        you the banner code to add to your site.
    </p>

    <p>
        Before joining, please also have a look at the
        <a href="/code-of-conduct">Code of Conduct</a>. It's there to help keep
        Spankscuary a welcoming, useful neighbourhood rather than to make joining
        complicated.
    </p>

    <h3>WordPress</h3>

    <p>
        Once you've received confirmation that your site has been added to the
        Spankscuary member list, add the navigation banner to your site.
    </p>

    <p>
        In WordPress, edit the page, sidebar, footer, or widget area where you'd like
        the banner to appear. Add a <strong>Custom HTML</strong> block or widget,
        then paste in the two lines of code shown below.
    </p>

    <p>
        Save or update the page, then test <strong>Previous</strong>,
        <strong>Random</strong>, and <strong>Next</strong>. The banner identifies
        your site automatically, so you don't need to edit the links when new members
        join the ring.
    </p>

    <p>
        Put it somewhere readers can find it. A sidebar or footer is a good choice,
        but the bottom of a homepage works too.
    </p>

